{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed flat would fail&nbsp;to comply with the internal space standards for a 2-person, 3-bedroom flat, resulting in a sense of enclosure and would fail to provide any external private amenity space further compounding the sense of being penned-in,&nbsp;presenting a sub-standard quality of accomodation, causing harm to the living standards of future occupiers. This&nbsp;is considered to be acceptable and contrary to:DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)Policy D6 and Table 3.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMD 1 and Part 6 of policy DMNE1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)",
    "In absence of marketing evidence to demonstrate the demand or viability of the office space within Barking Town Centre , the proposal would therefore result in the unjustified loss of office space within the key town centre location which is considered to be acceptable and&amp;nbsp;contrary to:The&amp;nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2023)Policy E1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy SP5 of the&amp;nbsp;the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)."
  ],
